    "name": "llm 0.32rc2",
    "plainTextLength": 1363,
    "plainTextPreview": "Release: llm 0.32rc2\n\nHot on the heels of RC1, this fixes a dependency issue and also adds two neat new features:\n\nThe default model for users who have not set their own default is now GPT-5.6 Luna. It was previously GPT-4o mini. Luna is a much better and more recent model, albeit slightly more expensive - $0.20 per million input tokens and $1.20 per million output tokens, compared to $0.15/$0.60 "
  },
  "blockKindCounts": {
    "blockquote": 1,
    "codeBlock": 1,
    "list": 1,
    "paragraph": 8
  },
  "document": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "runs": [
          {
            "link": null,
            "styles": [
              "bold"
            ],
            "text": "Release:"
          },
          {
            "link": null,
            "styles": [],
            "text": " "
          },
          {
            "link": "https://github.com/simonw/llm/releases/tag/0.32rc2",
            "styles": [],
            "text": "llm 0.32rc2"
          }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
      },
      {
        "runs": [
          {
            "link": null,
            "styles": [],
            "text": "Hot on the heels of "
          },
          {
            "link": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/30/llm-rc1/",
            "styles": [],
            "text": "RC1"
          },
          {
            "link": null,
            "styles": [],
            "text": ", this fixes a dependency issue and also adds two neat new features:"
          }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "items": [
              [
                {
                  "runs": [
                    {
                      "link": null,
                      "styles": [],
                      "text": "The default model for users who have not set their own default is now "
                    },
                    {
                      "link": null,
                      "styles": [],
                      "text": "GPT-5.6 Luna"
                    },
                    {
                      "link": null,
                      "styles": [],
                      "text": ". It was previously "
                    },
                    {
                      "link": null,
                      "styles": [],
                      "text": "GPT-4o mini"
                    },
                    {
                      "link": null,
                      "styles": [],
                      "text": ". Luna is a much better and more recent model, albeit slightly more expensive - $0.20 per million input tokens and $1.20 per million output tokens, compared to $0.15/$0.60 for 4o mini. You can switch back to 4o mini using "
                    },
                    {
                      "link": null,
                      "styles": [],
                      "text": "llm models default gpt-4o-mini"
                    },
                    {
                      "link": null,
                      "styles": [],
                      "text": ", or switch to "
                    },
                    {
                      "link": null,
                      "styles": [],
                      "text": "GPT-5 nano"
                    },
                    {
                      "link": null,
                      "styles": [],
                      "text": ", an even cheaper default model ($0.05/$0.40), using "
                    },
                    {
                      "link": null,
                      "styles": [],
                      "text": "llm models default gpt-5-nano"
                    },
                    {
                      "link": null,
                      "styles": [],
                      "text": ". "
                    },
                    {
                      "link": null,
                      "styles": [],
                      "text": "#1576"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "runs": [
                    {
                      "link": null,
                      "styles": [],
                      "text": "New "
                    },
                    {
                      "link": null,
                      "styles": [],
                      "text": "llm openai endpoint"
                    },
                    {
                      "link": null,
                      "styles": [],
                      "text": " command for running prompts, chats and model listings against arbitrary OpenAI-compatible endpoints without first configuring a model. These calls are not logged. "
                    },
                    {
                      "link": null,
                      "styles": [],
                      "text": "#1565"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph"
                }
              ]
            ],
            "ordered": false,
            "type": "list"
          }
        ],
        "type": "blockquote"
      },
      {
        "runs": [
          {
            "link": null,
            "styles": [],
            "text": "The "
          },
          {
            "link": null,
            "styles": [
              "code"
            ],
            "text": "llm openai endpoint"
          },
          {
            "link": null,
            "styles": [],
            "text": " command is "
          },
          {
            "link": null,
            "styles": [
              "italic"
            ],
            "text": "really"
          },
          {
            "link": null,
            "styles": [],
            "text": " cool. I got frustrated at the lack of an obvious CLI tool for trying out prompts against arbitrary OpenAI Chat Completions imitation endpoints, so I decided to add that to LLM itself."
          }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
      },
      {
        "runs": [
          {
            "link": null,
            "styles": [],
            "text": "You don't even have to install LLM to use this. Here's a "
          },
          {
            "link": null,
            "styles": [
              "code"
            ],
            "text": "uvx"
          },
          {
            "link": null,
            "styles": [],
            "text": " one-liner for running a prompt - with tools - against an "
          },
          {
            "link": "https://lmstudio.ai",
            "styles": [],
            "text": "LM Studio"
          },
          {
            "link": null,
            "styles": [],
            "text": " local model:"
          }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
      },
      {
        "language": null,
        "text": "uvx --pre llm openai endpoint http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1 \\\n  T llm_version -T llm_time --td \\\n  -m google/gemma-4-31b 'what is the current LLM version? And the time?'\n",
        "type": "codeBlock"
      },
      {
        "runs": [
          {
